<body>
# Add a TUI slash command

Steps to add a new `/command` handled natively by the Textual UI:

1. Add the command name to `_TUI_SLASH_COMMANDS` in `novacode_cli/tui/app.py` (autocomplete).
2. Add an `elif cmd == "<name>":` branch in `_run_slash` that calls a new `_run_<name>` handler.
3. Implement `_run_<name>` — render via native widgets / `self._log`, never `console.print` (it corrupts the TUI).
4. Add a one-line entry to the `/help` text.
5. Verify: `uv run pytest tests/test_tui_app.py -k routing`.
</body>
